      ":question/problem": "Express $3\\log_{2} (x) + 2\\log_{2} (y)$ as a single logarithm.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the power rule for logarithms, we can rewrite both terms:\n\n$$\n3\\log_{2} (x) + 2\\log_{2} (y)=\\log_{2}\\left(x^{3}\\right)+\\log_{2}\\left(y^{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, using the product rule, we combine the two terms:\n\n$$\n3\\log_{2} (x) + 2\\log_{2} (y)=\\log_{2} (x^{3}y^{2}).\n$$",
